  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 20 actions (src/actions.ts, one setActionDefinitions call) and 12 feedbacks (src/feedbacks.ts, one setFeedbackDefinitions call): 11 boolean and 1 advanced (sourceSignalState). Nothing is generated per model; the dropdown contents are built from the device state when the module (re)registers its definitions.",
    "Most dropdowns are filled at runtime from the connected device (screens, layers, presets, layer presets, inputs, crop sources, input backups). They carry choicesNote and valueType instead of choices; only the fixed lists (Toggle/Enable, load destination, bring-to, test patterns, spacing, speed, position) are closed. Screen ids are numbers (screenId), screen selections in multidropdowns of ftb/freeze and the screen feedbacks use the guid string.",
    "Where options default to the first screen (takeSingleScreen, takeMultipleScreen, setTestPattern, the screen feedbacks), the source default is evaluated at registration and not recorded as a fixed default. applyLayerPreset uses self.screens[0].screenId as the default of its layer preset dropdown (src/actions.ts:548), which is a screen id, not a layer preset id.",
    "Connection (src/main.ts, src/config.ts, src/services): config fields host (Regex.IP, required) and deviceSn (dropdown of discovered devices, default \"Default\"). The module discovers devices, logs in through an HTTP client (http://<host>:<apiPort> or https on 19998) and opens a WebSocket to wss://<host>:19998/unico/v1/ucenter/ws for state updates (src/services/WebSocketClient.ts:43). Ports other than 19998 come from the device list; they were not verified.",
    "Load destination ids: loadPreset, bringTo/layer \"Where\" and the feedbacks use 4 for preview and 2 for program (LoadIn in src/interfaces/Preset.ts), but toggleGlobalLoadPreset uses 0/1/2 (Toggle/Preview/Program).",
    "Visibility conditions use isVisibleExpression (base 1.12+); they are recorded as written in visibleWhen. selectLayer calls getLayerSelectionOptions(self, false), so its fields keep a condition on the missing option useSelected.",
    "ftb option ids: 0 is labelled Enable and 1 Disable, and the module passes !!option to ApiClient.ftb, which sends enable = 1 for true; the effective result on a device was not tested. In ApiClient.ftb the check uses the global object (`if (global)`), which is always truthy, so the toggle branch is never used.",
    "Presets and variables are not catalogued. Built on @companion-module/base ^1.12.1: options do not support expressions. The manifest version is 0.0.0, the package.json version is 2.2.9; legacy id pixelhue-fseries."
  ]
}
